{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I.</b> These too are the words of the prophet concerning himself:" "<b>I said.</b> In my heart:" "<b>In vain I have labored.</b> That I wearied my soul to rebuke Israel, and they did not listen:" "<b>Yet my judgment.</b> Is with HaShem, that He will give me reward for my labor. And likewise <i>ופעולתי</i> (and my recompense), as in <i>ולא תלין פעולת שכיר</i> (Leviticus 19:13):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:40.605485712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}